From 293ba597b7ab9c86e0d7f90bcd2005aeae9cc910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:37:54 -0400
Subject: Stop the shortcuts dialog from reporting a binding loop on every
 launch

Omawrite 0.5.0 builds the Ctrl+? "Keyboard shortcuts" Dialog with a bare
`contentItem: Label { ... }`. Under the Material style, Dialog.qml derives
implicitWidth from the content item's implicit width, and a custom content
item feeds that straight back into the popup's own sizing, so QML logs

  qrc:/Main.qml:332:5: QML Dialog: Binding loop detected for property
  "implicitWidth": qrc:/qt-project.org/imports/QtQuick/Controls/Material/Dialog.qml:14:5

four times at window creation, before the dialog is ever opened. It is
cosmetic (the dialog renders and sizes correctly) but it is emitted to the
terminal, or to journald when stderr is not a TTY, on every single launch.

Declaring the Label as a child of the Dialog instead lets the default content
item (a Pane) size to it through its contentWidth tracking, which does not
re-enter the implicitWidth binding. Measured offscreen with Qt 6.11.2: the
dialog's implicit size is identical (269.6 x 456) and the warning count drops
from 2 to 0. Wrapping the Label in a Column while keeping `contentItem:` does
NOT help; the loop is in the custom-content-item path itself.

The test guards it: shortcutsDialogHasNoBindingLoop loads Main.qml, opens the
dialog and fails on any "Binding loop detected" message. It fails against the
unpatched dialog (2 loops) and passes with this change.

Upstream: https://github.com/omacom/omawrite (unfixed on main as of 2026-09-17;
PR text drafted in upstream-pr-shortcuts-dialog-binding-loop.md).
Retires when: upstream ships the shortcuts dialog without the loop in pkgver > 0.5.0

diff -ruN a/src/Main.qml b/src/Main.qml

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

